# `power::pu`

Converts a value to per unit.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series power::pu(const pluss::Series& value, double base);
```

## What It Does

Divides a physical value by a base: `value / base`. The base is the one of the quantity, for example `Base::power` for power, `zbase` for impedance.

## Parameters

`value`
: The physical values, any shape.

`base`
: The base of the quantity.

## Returns

The per-unit values, the same shape as `value`.

## Errors

Throws `std::invalid_argument` for a base that is not finite and positive.

## Interpretation and Use

Convert once at the boundary of a study and keep everything inside in per unit.

